//? Title: Random-hyperplane locality-sensitive hashing
//? Subtitle: Actual signatures, candidates and the original cosine-search workload
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Random hyperplanes give nearby nonzero directions a higher probability of
agreeing on a sign bit. Concatenating bits and searching several tables trades
candidate count against missed neighbors. We retain the original collision
experiment and2000-by30 near-duplicate workload, expose actual query decisions,
and distinguish fewer cosine evaluations from the implementation’s total query
cost.
)

\toc

> A tiny actual signature and candidate search

For a nonzero vector x and a sampled plane normal r, assign bit one when
dot(r,x) is nonnegative, otherwise zero. Exact zero maps to one in this
implementation. A table concatenates k such bits into an unsigned key. Query
only the matching key in each table, suppress duplicate input identities, and
choose the first strict maximum cosine among encountered candidates. It can miss
the exact neighbor or find no candidates; it is not an exact search certificate.

The tiny example uses three two-dimensional directions, two tables, two bits
each and seed7. Its diagram/table show actual stored-plane signs, real keys and
actual bucket visits. The trace is emitted during one producing query, rather
than replaying signatures or recomputing candidates for the illustration.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lsh_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::algorithms::CosineLSH index({{1, 0}, {0, 1}, {-1, 0}}, 2, 2, 7);
    auto t = index.query_trace({1, .1});
    std::print("| actual table | actual bit | actual deciding dot | actual bit1 | scaled fallback |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto &p : t.projections)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", p.table, p.bit, p.dot,
                   p.nonnegative, p.scaled);
    std::print("\n| actual visiting table | actual input identity | duplicate | actual new cosine or " "duplicate placeholder0 | strict winner update |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &c : t.candidates)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", c.table, c.id, c.duplicate,
                   c.similarity, c.new_best);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("q", {0, 0}, "Actual query\n(1,0.1)").node("key", {6, 0},
                                                      std::format(
                                                      "Actual table0 key\n{}",
                                                      t.buckets.front().signature)).node("result", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual winner id{}\nexamined {}", t.analysis.best, t.analysis.examined)).edge("q", "key").edge("key", "result");
    d.save_svg("build/lsh_tiny.svg");
}
```
