> Why the ideal collision law is angular

For two nonzero directions separated by angle theta in[0,pi], only their spanned
plane matters. Isotropic random normal orientation separates their signs on a
fraction theta/pi of directions, so single-bit agreement has probability
p=1−theta/pi. With k independent bits per table, all-bit agreement has
probability p^k. With L independent tables, at least one matching table has
ideal probability1−(1−p^k)^L. This is a collision probability for one pair under
ideal independent planes, not the probability that a finite candidate search
returns the exact nearest neighbor.

The original experiment samples20000 independent two-dimensional Gaussian planes
at angles0,20,...,180 degrees, using mt19937_64 seed3. The native study then
continues the very same generator stream for the original indexed data and
queries. The displayed agreement counts are measured, while the reference curve
is the isotropic law. No calibration or deterministic finite-sample equality is
claimed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lsh_collision.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::lsh_original_study();
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    std::print("| prescribed degrees | actual agreeing planes | actual trials | actual agreement fraction | " "ideal isotropic probability |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : s.angles) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.degrees, r.agreements,
                   r.trials, r.empirical, r.theory);
        x.push_back(r.degrees);
        y.push_back(r.empirical);
        z.push_back(r.theory);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, z, "ideal law", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, y, "actual agreement",
                                                       {37, 99, 235}, 5).y_limits(-.05, 1.3).title("Original seeded random-plane collision experiment").x_label("prescribed angle in degrees").y_label("single-bit sign agreement fraction").save_svg("build/lsh_collision.svg");
}
```
