\caption(Original20000-plane angular agreement controls.)
\alttext(Measured agreement is compared with the ideal isotropic law, retaining actual seeded counts instead of asserting exact finite-sample equality.)

> Original2000-by30 approximate-neighbor workload

Continue the original seed3 stream after the collision experiment:2000 Gaussian
points in30 dimensions, then200 queries made by adding independent
standard-deviation0.3 noise to sampled source rows. The index uses15 tables,14
bits each and its own seed99. The exact baseline scans every indexed row by
cosine and keeps its first strict maximum. The approximate result comes from the
actual collided candidates. Recall compares these actual identities, rather than
assuming the planted source is always the exact nearest neighbor.

The native helper performs both searches and returns their actual outcomes. This
synthetic workload is designed to test angular near-duplicate retrieval; it is
not a measured guarantee for arbitrary embeddings or a real-data benchmark.
Candidate counts measure saved cosine evaluations, not elapsed-time speedup.
Standard-library Gaussian/uniform distribution mappings affect exact seeded
fixtures across toolchains.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lsh_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::lsh_original_study();
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::size_t hits = 0, examined = 0, missing = 0;
    std::print("| actual query index | sampled source | actual exact winner | actual approximate winner or " "SIZE_MAX | actual distinct examined | actual exact cosine | actual approximate cosine or " "sentinel |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < s.queries.size(); ++i) {
        auto &r = s.queries[i];
        hits += r.exact == r.approximate;
        examined += r.examined;
        missing += r.approximate == SIZE_MAX;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, r.source,
                   r.exact, r.approximate, r.examined, r.exact_similarity,
                   r.approximate_similarity);
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(r.examined);
    }
    std::print("\nActual indexed rows {}; dimension {}; queries {}; exact-winner recall {}; mean distinct " "examined {}; no-candidate outcomes {}.\n",
               s.data.size(), s.data.front().size(), s.queries.size(),
               double(hits) / s.queries.size(),
               double(examined) / s.queries.size(), missing);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual candidates", {37, 99, 235}, 3).title(
        "Original near-duplicate workload: actual cosine evaluations").x_label(
        "actual original query index").y_label("actual distinct candidates examined").save_svg("build/lsh_original.svg");
}
```
