> Verification and references

Native tests inspect every actual query projection against stored coefficients,
every real bucket against insertion-order signatures, all candidate
duplicate/winner decisions, exact work/capture counts, owned input and
index-copy lifetimes, zero vectors, zero/64-bit and zero-table controls, no
candidates, complete finite guards and extreme/subnormal cosine scaling.
Existing seeded recall and angle-agreement tests remain. The ten-report batch
passes 95 CTest cases, 30 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 121 compiled
and executed public examples, 601/601 scoped documentation definitions and 11
representative hovers. Independent integer, Fraction, graph, string and NumPy
references verify 82,729 records, including the complete original seeded LSH
study. Frozen comparisons preserve ordinary legacy results; malformed-input,
sentinel-collision, ownership and explicit-budget corrections are documented
above. Thirteen checkout headers and thirteen installed headers compile
independently, and an installed-header native consumer links and runs. Each
complete report program runs against the checkout library; all four native
figures are reviewed and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed results and
image bytes. Batch receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-214-223/`.

M. S. Charikar(2002),
[Similarity Estimation Techniques from Rounding Algorithms|https://doi.org/10.1145/509907.509965],
Proceedings of STOC,380–388. Its angular collision construction motivates the
index; the dense visited array, finite arithmetic, owned storage and measured
workload behavior are specific to this implementation.
